the LOINC copyright statement is reproduced in full.

Bundle members and their LOINC sources:

  loinc_axis.csv          — derived from LoincTableCore.csv, filtered
                            to STATUS=ACTIVE and reduced to columns
                            LOINC_NUM, COMPONENT, PROPERTY, TIME_ASPCT,
                            SYSTEM, SCALE_TYP, METHOD_TYP, STATUS,
                            LONG_COMMON_NAME.
  loinc_skip.txt          — LOINC codes excluded from resolve (non-
                            clinical CLASS / PHENX / DOC / SURVEY,
                            DEPRECATED / DISCOURAGED STATUS).
  loinc_demote.txt        — LOINC codes soft-demoted in sort
                            (LABORDERS.ONTOLOGY abstract codes,
                            TRIAL STATUS).
  loinc_rank_bonus.npy    — row-aligned float32 tie-breaker cosine
                            bonus, derived from LoincTable/Loinc.csv
                            COMMON_TEST_RANK column.
  loinc_alias_index.npz   — multilingual lexical alias → corpus-row
                            inverted index, derived from
                            LoincTable/Loinc.csv (COMPONENT,
                            RELATEDNAMES2, SHORTNAME, DisplayName,
                            CONSUMER_NAME) and all AccessoryFiles/
                            LinguisticVariants/*.csv.

Source: LOINC release 2.82 (LoincTable/, LoincTableCore/, AccessoryFiles/).

This used to read "2.82 or later". Section 9 of the LOINC license asks each
copy to carry "the appropriate version number of the Licensed Materials", and a
range is not one. It is determinable, and now determined: of the 3,081 codes
ACTIVE in 2.83 that this bundle does not carry, 3,078 were first released in
2.83 — so the cut is 2.82 exactly. `mirobody.BUNDLE_VERSION` reports it at
runtime.

Full LOINC license: https://loinc.org/license/
